course: dictionary
lesson: 11404
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to official writing, such as rules, letters from school, signs and tests. Accordance is one of these words. You will almost only meet it in the phrase in accordance with, so learn the phrase as one chunk.
explain: «The bins are emptied in accordance with the council timetable.» The clue is the timetable, a plan with set times. So in accordance with means following a plan, which is the same as matching it.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning: «The bins are emptied following the council timetable.» It still makes sense. Accordance means agreement, so the bin day and the timetable agree with each other.
fact: Accordance means agreement, and it is used mostly in the phrase in accordance with.
fact: «In accordance with» means following, obeying or matching a rule, wish or plan.
fact: «The school bus leaves in accordance with the timetable.» The bus follows the timetable.
fact: «She baked the cake in accordance with her grandmother's wishes.» She did it the way her grandmother wanted.
fact: Words like accordance often appear in rules, letters and signs, so look for the clue that tells you who made the rule or plan.
exercise: «The library is open in accordance with the posted hours.» What does in accordance with mean here? | Ignoring the posted hours | *Following the posted hours | Painting the posted hours | Losing the posted hours
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «in accordance with the rules»? | Making up new rules | Forgetting the rules | *Following the rules | Breaking the rules
exercise: «Sam painted the fence in accordance with his mum's plan.» What does this tell you? | Sam threw the paint away | Sam ignored the plan | *Sam followed his mum's plan | Sam had no paint
test: «The cake was baked in accordance with the recipe.» What does this tell you? | *It was made by following the recipe | It was made without any recipe | It was burnt by mistake | It was made by a robot
test: Which sentence shows accordance meaning agreement? | The map was blue. | *The plan and the map were in accordance: they matched. | The plan was lost in the rain. | The map was torn in two.
exam: «The club changed its rules in accordance with the members' wishes.» What does this tell you? | The club closed down | The members wrote angry letters about the rules | *The rules were changed to match what the members wanted | The rules were never changed
